+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+## State
+
+Project is fresh off a single initial commit (`828713e`). `RIGGING.md` is fitted out.
+No production code exists (`js/` directory absent). Assets spec and template are in `assets/`.
+
+## Specs authored
+
+Five feature files written under `features/`:
+- `todo-core.feature` — create, toggle, remove, counter, clear-completed, no-todos state
+- `todo-editing.feature` — double-click edit, save, discard, empty destroy
+- `todo-toggle-all.feature` — mark all as complete, state reflection
+- `todo-persistence.feature` — localStorage key, writes, reload restoration
+- `todo-routing.feature` — hash routing for all/active/completed, selected class, reload persistence
+
+## watchbill.json
+
+Four ordered watches:
+1. Core + Persistence (foundational data layer)
+2. Editing (depends on core CRUD)
+3. Toggle All (depends on core CRUD)
+4. Routing (depends on core CRUD, filter behaviour)
+
+## Known gaps / open questions
+
+- Persistence is coupled with core CRUD in watch 1 since the model needs localStorage from the start.
+- The `@planks(...)` annotations on production seams will be added by Crew when production code is written.
+- Verification tier: the `RIGGING.md` already uses `happy-dom` which is the cheapest DOM tier. Cucumber + happy-dom verification will be authored by QM.
+- No `@contract` or `@conformance` scenarios needed at this stage — the app has no schema or method contract beyond behaviour.
+
+## Next
+
+Dispatch QM when the user confirms. Context MUST clear before QM dispatch per the Context bulkhead Article.
\ No newline at end of file
