+Feature: Todo Core Operations
+  As a user
+  I want to create, view, and manage todos
+  So that I can track what I need to do
+
+  Background:
+    Given the page is loaded
+
+  Rule: No-todos state
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer are hidden when no todos exist
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    Then "#main" is not visible
+    And "#footer" is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer are shown when a todo exists
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    Then "#main" is visible
+    And "#footer" is visible
+
+  Rule: New todo creation
+
+  Scenario: Create a new todo by pressing Enter
+    When I type "Buy groceries" into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the new item has title "Buy groceries"
+    And the new item is not completed
+    And the new-todo input is cleared
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace from new todo title
+    When I type "   Walk the dog   " into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the new item has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Empty input does not create a todo
+    When I type "   " into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Input is focused on page load
+    Then the new-todo input has focus
+
+  Rule: Item completion
+
+  Scenario: Toggle a todo as completed
+    Given I create a todo with text "Read a book"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Read a book"
+    Then the item "Read a book" has class "completed"
+    And the toggle checkbox for "Read a book" is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle a completed todo back to active
+    Given I create a todo with text "Read a book"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Read a book"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Read a book"
+    Then the item "Read a book" does not have class "completed"
+    And the toggle checkbox for "Read a book" is not checked
+
+  Rule: Todo removal
+
+  Scenario: Remove a todo by clicking the destroy button
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    When I click the destroy button for "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Rule: Remaining count
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows remaining items count
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
+    And I create a todo with text "Read"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo-count text is "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter pluralization for single item
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo-count text is "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter pluralization for zero items
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    Then the todo-count text is "0 items left"
+
+  Rule: Clear completed
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes all completed todos
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    When I click "Clear completed"
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the remaining item has title "Walk dog"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no completed todos exist
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    Then the clear-completed button is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is shown when completed todos exist
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the clear-completed button is visible
\ No newline at end of file
