@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+Feature: Todo Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to be saved across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the page is loaded
+
+  Rule: localStorage writes
+
+  Scenario: Creating a todo persists it to localStorage
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then localStorage contains a todo with title "Buy milk" and completed false
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo persists the completed state
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage contains a todo with title "Buy milk" and completed true
+
+  Scenario: Deleting a todo removes it from localStorage
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    When I click the destroy button for "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage does not contain a todo with title "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Editing a todo persists the new title
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy oat milk"
+    And I press Enter in the edit input
+    Then localStorage contains a todo with title "Buy oat milk" and completed false
+    And localStorage does not contain a todo with title "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: localStorage key format
+
+  Scenario: Uses the correct localStorage key
+    Then localStorage has a key starting with "todos-"
+
+  Rule: Data reload
+
+  Scenario: Todos are restored from localStorage on page load
+    Given localStorage has a stored todo with title "Buy milk" and completed false
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the new item has title "Buy milk"
+    And the new item is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit input to "Buy oat milk"
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the item "Buy milk" does not have class "editing"
