+Feature: Todo Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter todos by status using URL hash routes
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the page is loaded
+
+  Rule: Default route shows all
+
+  Scenario: All todos are shown by default
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    And the route is "#/"
+    Then the todo list contains 2 items
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only uncompleted todos
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    When the route is "#/active"
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the remaining item has title "Walk dog"
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    When the route is "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the remaining item has title "Buy milk"
+    And the remaining item is completed
+
+  Rule: Selected class on filter links
+
+  Scenario: The active filter link has the selected class
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    When the route is "#/active"
+    Then the filter link for "Active" has class "selected"
+    And the filter link for "All" does not have class "selected"
+    And the filter link for "Completed" does not have class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: The all filter link has the selected class on default route
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    When the route is "#/"
+    Then the filter link for "All" has class "selected"
+
+  Rule: Item update within filter
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo in active filter removes it from view
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
+    And the route is "#/active"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Walk dog"
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo in completed filter removes it from view
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    And I create a todo with text "Walk dog"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    And the route is "#/completed"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Rule: Filter state persistence
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists on reload
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    And the route is "#/active"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the filter link for "Active" has class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter persists on reload
+    Given I create a todo with text "Buy milk"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    And the route is "#/completed"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the filter link for "Completed" has class "selected"
+    And the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the remaining item has title "Buy milk"
